{"id": "EUVD-2026-96595", "enisaUuid": "4ed5bda5-5d4a-3aa7-92a1-f930c8ac45a1", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the SysTenantController GET /sys/tenant/getTenantPackApplyUsers endpoint that allows any authenticated user to read tenant administrator applications. Low-privileged attackers can iterate the tenantId parameter to retrieve pending applicants' usernames, real names, phone numbers and departments for any tenant.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T19:54:10", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_tenant_ownership_and_pack_approval.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/system/controller/SysTenantController.java#L816-L820", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-gettenantpackapplyusers-endpoint"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108656", "GHSA-xp5m-3f3f-ffgp"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3f98f3f3-5a31-3369-90bc-dfab6d45c1d8", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e4dad9de-24b0-32d4-9714-67dae4c7f072", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}